list.item:
Severe renal insufficiency when renal function status cannot be monitored [see Warnings and Precautions (
                              5.11, 5.14
                           )]

text.paragraph:
Sulfamethoxazole and Trimethoprim Injection is contraindicated in pediatric patients younger than two months of age because of the potential risk of bilirubin displacement and kernicterus [see Contraindications (
                                 4
                              )].
